>Anyting you #offer at a non-coaligned altar, the two gods will fight for
>control of the altar.  The higher your experience level, the better the
>chance that your god will win.  By the time you're level 7 or 8, the odds
>are quite good.  In the meantime, just remember where the altar is and don't
>worry about it too much.

Close.  You can't offer a unicorn of the same alignment as an alter to
convert it.  In other words, if you are nuetral and want to convert a
lawful altar, you can't do the conversion with a white unicorn.  Convert
the altar with something other than a unicorn then sacrifice your unicorn
corpse.  Actually, a unicorn not aligned with you or the altar may work.
I've never tried it.

Sacrificing a co-aligned unicorn corpse at a non-coaligned altar is
something everyone should do at least once...
